# CASM Phase 11 WP61 Increment 4 trusted reference: casmfa2p
#
# Independently hand-assembled from the casmfa2p fixture source in
# cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake. NOT produced by CASM. Proves
# CASM_PARSER_STMT_FORCE_ABS (parser.s:562-575) holds across a genuine
# two-pass real assembly for a FORWARD symbol reference whose resolved
# value lands in the zero-page range ($00-$FF): "LDA TARGET" must emit as
# 3-byte absolute ($AD lo hi), never shrink to 2-byte zero-page ($A5 lo),
# even though TARGET's actual resolved value ($0013) would fit zero-page
# if it were a literal. Complements the existing p1back1 unit-level
# evidence (single measure pass, backward reference,
# brain/reviews and cmake/GenerateCasmTestFixtures.cmake's own p1back1
# block) with an end-to-end proof in the opposite (forward) direction.
#
# Source (.ORG $0010):
#   LDA TARGET
#   TARGET NOP (label TARGET on the NOP line)
#
# CasmPc starts at $0010. TARGET is not yet defined when "LDA TARGET" is
# first measured (a genuine forward reference) -- CASM_EXPR_FLAG_SYMBOL_
# DERIVED is set the moment the resolver call succeeds with C clear,
# regardless of whether the symbol itself resolved, and
# CASM_PARSER_STMT_FORCE_ABS is derived from it unconditionally before the
# resolved/unresolved branch (parser.s:562-570). So Pass 1 sizes "LDA
# TARGET" as 3-byte absolute without yet knowing TARGET's value, and Pass 2
# -- which re-parses the statement from scratch, not reusing Pass 1's
# record -- must independently re-derive the identical classification and
# commit the same 3-byte absolute opcode to the real output. TARGET is
# defined immediately after, at $0010 + 3 = $0013.
#
# Hand assembly:
#   10 00              PRG load-address header ($0010, little-endian)
#   AD 13 00           LDA $0013                    (absolute, FORCE_ABS)
#   EA                 TARGET: NOP
#
# bytes: 6
# sha256: 9d5821446dd4e9521d402e1b0babe0ff5a2287e261355b59e65d334237f48a4f
# source_sha256: casmfa2p.seq=77717a44eb271d0d9421d2be52fcf2f1359b2fd91890b04fd73c3c5a2f2764a9
# Independent byte derivation reviewed and approved by the user 2026-09-02
#   (WP3 batch 3 -- brain/reviews/2026-09-02-casm-byte-oracle-wp3-batch3-r6-relocation.md).

10 00
AD 13 00
EA
